{"name":"Taffeta Darling","hex":"#af797e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"taffeta","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A crisp, smooth woven fabric made from silk or synthetic fibers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taffeta"},{"term":"darling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Often used as an affectionate term of address: a person who is very dear to one.","A person who is kind, sweet, etc., and thus lovable; a pet, a sweetheart; also, an animal or thing which is cute and lovable."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very dear; beloved, cherished, favourite.","Very cute or lovable; adorable, charming, sweet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/darling"}],"entries":[{"title":"Taffeta","blocks":[{"text":"Taffeta is a crisp, smooth, plain woven fabric made from silk, nylon, cuprammonium rayons, acetate, or polyester. The word came into Middle English via Old French and Old Italian, which borrowed the Persian word tāfta (تافته), which means \"silk\" or \"linen cloth\". As clothing, it is used in ball gowns, wedding dresses, and corsets, and in interior decoration, for curtains or wallcovering. It tends to yield a stiff cloth with a starched appearance that holds its shape better than many other fabrics and does not sag or drape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Woman%27s_Dress_LACMA_M.2007.211.35_%283_of_7%29.jpg/330px-Woman%27s_Dress_LACMA_M.2007.211.35_%283_of_7%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taffeta"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Pink_evening_coat_designed_by_Sybil_Connolly_-_Full_Lenght_Front.jpg/500px-Pink_evening_coat_designed_by_Sybil_Connolly_-_Full_Lenght_Front.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Pink_evening_coat_designed_by_Sybil_Connolly_-_Full_Lenght_Front.jpg/1280px-Pink_evening_coat_designed_by_Sybil_Connolly_-_Full_Lenght_Front.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Pink_evening_coat_designed_by_Sybil_Connolly_-_Full_Lenght_Front.jpg/500px-Pink_evening_coat_designed_by_Sybil_Connolly_-_Full_Lenght_Front.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pink taffeta evening coat designed by Sybil Connolly","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APink_evening_coat_designed_by_Sybil_Connolly_-_Full_Lenght_Front.jpg"}],"sounds":{"taffeta":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/07/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-taffeta.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/07/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-taffeta.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-taffeta.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/07/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-taffeta.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-taffeta.wav.ogg"}],"darling":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/En-us-darling.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f0/En-us-darling.ogg/En-us-darling.ogg.mp3"}]}}}